            doses = "Tinea Corporis / Tinea Cruris:\n• 100 mg PO once daily for 15 days OR 200 mg PO once daily for 7 days.\n\nTinea Pedis / Tinea Manuum:\n• 100 mg PO once daily for 30 days OR 200 mg PO BID for 7 days.\n\nOnychomycosis (Pulse Therapy):\n• 200 mg PO BID (total 400 mg/day) for 1 week per month. (Fingernails: 2 pulses = 2 months; Toenails: 3 pulses = 3 months).\n\nPityriasis Versicolor:\n• 200 mg PO once daily for 7 days.\n\nVulvovaginal Candidiasis:\n• 200 mg PO BID for 1 day OR 200 mg PO once daily for 3 days.",
            administration = "Standard capsules MUST BE TAKEN IMMEDIATELY AFTER A FULL MEAL. Gastric acidity is absolutely essential for dissolution and absorption of standard itraconazole. Acid-reducing agents (PPIs, H2 blockers, antacids) drastically impair absorption. If co-administered with acid reducers, instruct patient to take with an acidic beverage (cola). (Newer Super-Bioavailable [SB] formulations can be taken with or without food).",
