            doses = "WHO Low-Osmolarity Formula (per Liter of reconstituted solution: Sodium 75 mmol/L, Chloride 65 mmol/L, Glucose 75 mmol/L, Potassium 20 mmol/L, Citrate 10 mmol/L; Total Osmolarity 245 mOsm/L).\n\nRehydration Therapy (First 4 Hours per WHO Plan B):\n• Weight <5 kg (<4 months): 200 - 400 mL.\n• Weight 5-7.9 kg (4-11 months): 400 - 600 mL.\n• Weight 8-10.9 kg (1-2 years): 600 - 800 mL.\n• Weight 11-15.9 kg (2-4 years): 800 - 1200 mL.\n• Weight 16-29.9 kg (5-14 years): 1200 - 2200 mL.\n• Adults (≥15 years): 2200 - 4000 mL.\n\nMaintenance (Ongoing Losses - WHO Plan A):\n• Children <2 years: 50-100 mL after every loose stool.\n• Children 2-9 years: 100-200 mL after every loose stool.\n• Adults & Adolescents ≥10 years: As much as wanted (usually 200-400 mL after every loose stool).",
